u2022 The `assertOpen(assetId)` hook is called by token contracts             during every `transfer()`.           \\u2022 Posterior values are scaled \\u00d71e18 (uint256 representation of             the rational probability produced by scorer.js).\",\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{\"assertOpen(bytes32)\":{\"details\":\"Example usage:           function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) external {               registry.assertOpen(keccak256(\\\"MyAsset\\\"));               _performTransfer(msg.sender, to, amount);           }\"},\"check(bytes32,uint256)\":{\"details\":\"If the asset is OPEN and posterior >= threshold, it trips to HALTED.         If already HALTED, the call is a no-op (absorbing state for UNAUTH).\"},\"registerAsset(bytes32,uint256,address)\":{\"params\":{\"assetId\":\"Arbitrary identifier (e.g. keccak256(\\\"RealT-Detroit-1\\\")).\",\"resetter\":\"Secondary address authorised to reset this asset's kernel.\",\"threshold\":\"Trip posterior in \\u00d71e18 units (e.g. 0.75e18 = 75%).\"}}},\"title\":\"AssetRegistry\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{\"assertOpen(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Hook called in every token transfer.  Reverts if HALTED.\"},\"check(bytes32,uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Called by TEEVerifier (or oracle) to advance the kernel state.\"},\"isOpen(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Returns true iff the asset kernel is in the OPEN state.\"},\"kernels(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Per-asset safety kernel.\"},\"registerAsset(bytes32,uint256,address)\":{\"notice\":\"Register a new asset with its own isolated safety kernel.\"},\"reset(bytes32)\":{\"notice\":\"Reset a tripped kernel.  Owner or the asset-level resetter only.\"},\"setThreshold(bytes32,uint256)\":{\"notice\":\"Update the trip threshold for an existing asset.\"}},\"notice\":\"Multi-asset registry \\u2014 each asset owns an isolated safety kernel.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"contracts/AssetRegistry.sol\":\"AssetRegistry\"},\"evmVersion\":\"shan